BrlTex Installation instructions

There are two ways to install BrlTex now, either with the install script or manual install. NOTE: Other packages, such 
as python and plasTeX, are written by other authors and may have different licenses.

Installation script
For this you will need python from www.python.org, and a copy of BrlTex from 
SVN.

To install, go to the BrlTex directory, and run install.py. This will download all other components and install them, 
if it is successful it will inform you that you can then run BrlTex.py. After this update it just by running 'svn 
update', you will not need to run install.py again. If it was unsuccessful, either you will need to try and 
work out what went wrong or follow the manual install instructions.

Manual install instructions
You will need python from www.python.org, plasTeX from http://plastex.sourceforge.net and nfbtrans from www.nfbnet.org/files/nfbtrans/NFBTR770.ZIP, as well as a 
copy of BrlTex from SVN.

Follow the install instructions for python. Now decompress plasTeX, and modify the file Entities.py in 
plasTeX/Base/LaTeX/. You need to comment out the last line of Entities.py, by putting a # at the beginning of the line. 
Now install plasTeX as usual. If you are running Windows put nfbtrans.exe in the BrlTex directory, otherwise follow the 
compile instructions for nfbtrans and move the executable from that into the BrlTex directory. Now you should be able to 
run BrlTex.py.


